  "behaviour": {
    "groundRallies": "Carts and Cogs follow normal ground rally paths and pause after arrival instead of silently entering or resuming another trade route. This also applies to explicit manual movement from authenticated humans.",
    "soloTradeRallies": "A release on a completed living non-hostile foreign Market or Dock assigns a trade target to the selected production group. Matching newly trained merchants use their own producing depot as home. Wrong unit/endpoint combinations and invalid targets remain ground rallies.",
    "depotApproach": "walk has an optional precise final approach. Only trade-route movement opts in; ordinary two-argument walks retain the previous tolerance. This removes the diagonal stall just outside the 1.1-tile delivery footprint.",
    "savedTargets": "Current-build saves serialize rally targets as node or Market/Dock building references. Unit, unrelated building and out-of-range references are rejected before replacing the world.",
    "authority": "The two-human HTTP fixture uses the production host, frame loop, paid market queues and rally dispatch for both teams. The multiplayer protocol still accepts ground rallies only; no remote trade-target command was added."
  },
